WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:01.613
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:01.613 --> 00:00:03.580
- Did y'all plan this?

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.870
You kind of like compliment each other.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.250
Did you plan it?
- No.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.350
- [Kelly Clarkson] You
compliment each other.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.236
You walked out and I was
like, nice earthy tones.

00:00:12.236 --> 00:00:13.069
(Lily and Jane laughing)

00:00:13.069 --> 00:00:15.250
I am so excited y'all are here.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.420
I'm such a big fan of both of you.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.647
- We're excited, too.

00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:18.855
- I literally.
- [Both] Very.

00:00:18.855 --> 00:00:22.010
- I've never rubbed
anything in my sister's face

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.460
and this will be the thing

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.814
that I just remind her of every Christmas.

00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:28.040
(audience clapping)
- Okay.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.730
- She's the one who
actually got me addicted

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.160
to your show when it first came on

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.870
and I was just like, oh my God.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.300
I loved y'all before, but
it's just such a great show.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.730
Congratulations on this show

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.946
being such a huge hit.
- Thank you.

00:00:37.946 --> 00:00:39.040
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.240
- So you've been doing
it and I wanna tell you

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.420
Jesse, over there, my singer I work with,

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.890
she's celebrating your
show with a martini.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.723
She loves you.

00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:51.020
- [Lily] Can I have some?

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.380
- Everybody kept going so professional.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.400
I was like, she's
usually, this is amazing.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.500
This is why we love Jesse.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.120
But also she wanted to celebrate y'all.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.050
We're all very excited and
honored that you're here.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:00:59.883
- Thanks.

00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:02.300
- Anyway, you've been doing
this show for seven years now.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.680
- It's the longest running
original Netflix show ever.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.860
- That's amazing.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.300
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.770
I know that y'all had to meet way before.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.430
So when did y'all first meet?

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.870
- Well, I was developing
a movie called "9 To 5",

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:18.708
It was not cast yet.
- Never heard of it.

00:01:18.708 --> 00:01:19.885
(all laughing)
(audience clapping)

00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:21.158
Never heard of it.

00:01:21.158 --> 00:01:23.133
- With your friend, Dolly.
- Yes.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:26.650
- But none of that existed,
Lily Tomlin, Dolly Parton.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.760
I wasn't a television person

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.420
and I was developing it as a dark comedy.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.630
And I heard Lily Tomlin is downtown LA

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.160
doing a one-woman show
called "Appearing Nightly"

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.230
and I went by myself.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:44.280
I was just knocked off my feet.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.370
I was totally smitten by her.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.350
And I first met her going
backstage and I said to myself,

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:53.180
I'm not making a movie about
secretaries unless she's in it.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.410
So I thought, we're gonna have

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.587
to change everything.
- I had a Steno pad,

00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.883
and I was like, we're taking shorthand,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.829
had a typewriter over here.
- That's why you got the job.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.640
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.920
So do you remember that, the
first time that y'all met?

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.660
- Yes, I was totally knocked over

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.941
because I was such a fan of Fonda's

00:02:09.941 --> 00:02:13.455
and I had a "Klute" hairdo and everything.

00:02:13.455 --> 00:02:14.363
(audience laughing)
- Love it.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.150
- So when she came back stage
it was really exciting for me.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.040
I think she was sort of trepidatious,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.607
but I was like "Can I get an autograph?"

00:02:26.987 --> 00:02:29.128
"Can you get a note to my mother?"

00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:30.590
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.070
- Asking for all the things?
It's amazing.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.520
Well, it must have been
cool working with Dolly.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.353
Were you kind of nervous

00:02:35.353 --> 00:02:37.450
'cause she'd never done
a big thing before?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.150
- Were you nervous?
- No.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.150
- I was nervous, but not because of her.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.930
This one, I was nervous 'cause of her.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.920
- Oh my God.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.400
- I love that, when you're
so inspired by someone

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.620
and you're willing to...
That's cool.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.140
- She wasn't sure if
I was gonna behave or?

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.297
(Kelly laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:02:53.297 --> 00:02:56.100
- Well that's like working
with Blake Shelton.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.530
That's what my life is
like on "The Voice".

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.490
So I'm like, what's he gonna say?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.440
So wait, is it true that
Dolly might actually appear

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.273
on "Grace and Frankie"?

00:03:03.273 --> 00:03:04.960
I heard that this was true.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.787
Okay.
(audience cheering)

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.713
I'm very excited.

00:03:09.713 --> 00:03:13.280
- We're very excited, that
was like the greatest.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.280
She's on our last episode,
we were just so excited

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.860
that the show was gonna
end with the three of us.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.800
- I know, that's what I'm saying.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.770
'Cause we really haven't
seen that, so that's amazing.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.820
And also her documentary is coming out

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.150
and "9 To 5", the anniversary of it.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.000
So it's like a lot of things
coming together at once.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.440
It's very cool.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.440
- The way she is in the last
episode is just perfect.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.700
I mean, you couldn't think of a better way

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.440
to have Dolly appear.
- [Kelly] What a tease.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.273
- I know it's a tease, but oh my god.

00:03:41.273 --> 00:03:42.540
- That was a great tease.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.430
- [Jane] Oh, it was so good.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.150
- Yeah, I'm a little upset about it.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.740
I'm like, wait what?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.770
So wait, we're just a few
weeks away from summer.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.560
- I'd like to be on a
show with Blake Shelton.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.330
- You would?
Oh my God.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.470
Actually, that would be...

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.310
You would love him and
it would be very funny

00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:00.110
what would come out of both
of your mouths at each other.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.060
Yes, he's very fun to work with.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.390
- Oh, he is?
- Do you wanna know why?

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.160
It's because probably how
much y'all loved working.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.060
This is why I love working.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.540
He and John, it's really
fun to work with people

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.670
that can put their ego aside
and just have a good time

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.750
and go in on each other and
you know you love each other

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.040
at the end of the day and you're good.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.245
That's why it's so fun.

00:04:17.245 --> 00:04:18.078
- That's great.

00:04:18.078 --> 00:04:19.160
That's good to here.
- There's nothing like it.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.330
'Cause I think it feels like
sometimes in this industry,

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:24.660
people can have doors up and
they're afraid to look silly

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.410
or afraid of what people
are not being credible

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.730
or afraid of all these things

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:32.720
and that fear, I think
really stifles creativity

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.840
and stifles a good time.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.272
- [Jane] I agree.

00:04:35.272 --> 00:04:37.850
- He was on "Reba" when I did her show.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.397
- I know, I knew that.

00:04:39.397 --> 00:04:40.830
- He was really adorable.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.498
- So you worked with him?

00:04:42.498 --> 00:04:43.810
You met him.
- Yeah, I did.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.340
- You never told me that.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.117
- Well, I don't tell you everything.

00:04:48.117 --> 00:04:51.214
(all laughing)

00:04:51.214 --> 00:04:53.131
- Wait a damned minute.

00:04:54.115 --> 00:04:56.198
I am really disappointed.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.860
You know, I have not
worn heels in two years.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.880
- Oh, that's the one
positive about the pandemic.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.690
- Much less strap on heels.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.540
So when we were headed here,

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.317
I said, "Lily, I've gotta hold
on to you when I come on."

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.963
See, I tell you everything.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:17.913
I'm never gonna wear heels again.

00:05:17.913 --> 00:05:20.103
- And you leave out run
ins with Blake Shelton.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.763
Congratulations on all
the success of the show.

00:05:25.799 --> 00:05:28.290
Is it hard to say goodbye
to these characters

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.680
that you've been playing?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.430
'Cause you feel like these
characters have kind of become

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.058
a little of you or a
little of you is in them.

00:05:34.058 --> 00:05:35.950
- Well you can see by
the way we're dressed

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.940
that would probably show you
that a lot of us are in them.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:39.773
(audience laughing)

00:05:39.773 --> 00:05:40.804
- A lot of them is in us.

00:05:40.804 --> 00:05:42.890
- A lot of them is in us.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.633
A lot of us is in them.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.417
Whichever way you cut it.
- It's a different show.

00:05:47.417 --> 00:05:49.550
(Kelly chuckling)

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.440
So are y'all afraid of the
characters, leaving them behind?

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.330
- Well, we cried.
I cried.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.520
She probably didn't cry.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.210
- I did cry.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.230
I cried more than you cried.
- Oh no, you didn't.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.740
I have a film to prove it.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.483
No, I cried more than she did.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.843
- She was crying because
a lot of the people,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.550
they were applauding us, you
know, but she was fearful

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.142
that they were applauding
because she was leaving.

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:19.725
(all laughing)

00:06:21.276 --> 00:06:23.810
How can you resist that?

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.894
- You were teed up.
- [Lily] Look at her.

00:06:25.894 --> 00:06:28.644
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.330
Get her a martini, Jesse.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.012
- Oh my God, it's not that.

00:06:33.012 --> 00:06:36.057
It's not anything so horrible.

00:06:36.057 --> 00:06:37.010
- No, it was sad.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.910
It was sad, we were together.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.713
There's also something to
be said for a regular job.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.280
- Very much so.
- Yeah.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.810
- Us being musicians,
literally we got this job

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:49.070
and then COVID hit and
all our musician friends

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.420
didn't have work for a couple years.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.450
We really lucked out 'cause all our people

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.300
are on the road and
nobody was able to work.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.710
So we get that.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:59.000
We had jobs during that
time, it was very cool.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.930
- I have to apologize for being so rude.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.600
It's just my-

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.141
- Ruthless.
You're ruthless.

00:07:06.141 --> 00:07:08.538
(all laughing)
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:07:08.538 --> 00:07:11.560
- No, I don't know when to shut up.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.580
- No, but that's why it's so awesome.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.970
This is what's awesome about Blake.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:20.040
See, you and Blake, I need
y'all to do a movie with Blake.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.700
You know what, if can you get him to work.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.000
- I'll do it.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.550
- That cowboy likes being on his ranch.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:29.530
He doesn't like to work, but
actually that would be...

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.000
When are y'all doing this
'cause I am excited as a fan.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.370
Y'all should do something, do a fun movie.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.460
Are you gonna do that?

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:37.680
- [Jane] Well.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.513
- Okay.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:40.703
I didn't know.

00:07:40.703 --> 00:07:42.540
- We've actually already done one

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:43.930
and we're gonna start another one.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:44.820
- Two movies.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.900
- Okay, I know, but are you gonna do one

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.879
based on these characters at all?

00:07:48.879 --> 00:07:49.712
- No.
- No.

00:07:49.712 --> 00:07:50.790
- Fine.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.110
(all laughing)

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.313
Fine, don't give the
people what they want.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.553
No, I just love these characters.

00:07:57.553 --> 00:07:59.460
They're just such a fun, fresh idea.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.230
- I agree, I think-

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.303
- How about a movie with Tom Brady?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.590
- [Kelly] Not too shabby.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.610
- Better watch out, Blake.

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.673
- [Kelly] So many
football jokes right now.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.260
- Really?

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.390
- Nevermind.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.223
So, wait.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.950
How would you describe the importance

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.600
of female friendships in your life?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.310
Because that's what I feel like,

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.500
literally Jess and I were just talking

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.280
before y'all came out here
and she was like, this show,

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.860
you have no idea what it meant for me

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.480
and I think for females in general.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.750
I have always had solid
female friendships.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:34.380
I feel like they're the
friendships, no offense to men,

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.550
but I can really go deep
and we can really talk

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:40.320
and just be very vulnerable
and work stuff out.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.610
Do you feel like that's been helpful

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.960
for you through your life?
- Yeah, totally.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.600
Male friendships are facing
outward side by side,

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:50.047
looking out, "Oh, look at her boobs."

00:08:50.047 --> 00:08:52.720
"God, what a great car."

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.950
And always gonna do a
touchdown, you know that.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.030
Women friendships are face to face.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.897
And it's like, "Can you help me?"

00:09:00.897 --> 00:09:02.697
"I'm really lost."

00:09:02.697 --> 00:09:03.530
"Can you help me?"

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.220
And you'll take me in your arms.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:07.820
We're not afraid to ask for help.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.840
We're not afraid to express vulnerability.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:14.500
We just drill down to kind of soul level

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.100
very fast, women do.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.400
- Do you think that's a
societal thing though?

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.750
I'm raised in the south.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.130
They're raised not to
do that, I feel like.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.160
- [Jane] That's right.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:23.993
- Which is a shame.

00:09:23.993 --> 00:09:26.853
- Don't express need, don't ask for help,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.310
keep it on the surface.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.500
It's one of the strengths-

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.790
- 'Cause you'll appear weak.
- Of women.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.180
That's right, is that
we're not afraid of that

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.860
and it's one of the things
that gives us strength.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.310
I'm sorry I'm doing all the talking.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.640
- That's all right.
- It's okay.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.441
- I've already lived it.

00:09:42.441 --> 00:09:45.024
(all laughing)

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.767
- That's true, actually.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.857
And that's the truth.

00:09:55.857 --> 00:09:57.430
- Oh my God.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.230
- Anyway, there's a Harvard
medical school study

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:03.120
that shows that for women,
lacking women friends

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.790
is as dangerous for
their health as smoking.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.623
- Wow.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.510
- There's a lot to be said
for women friendships.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:14.110
We just have to teach men how
to do friendship differently

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:15.713
and maybe there'd be fewer wars.

00:10:17.339 --> 00:10:18.780
- To say that it's okay to do it that way.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.090
Like I said, with the guys I grew up with,

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.060
I think they were taught to have barriers.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.310
- Oh yeah, they don't need anyone.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.531
- Have you had strong female
relationships your whole life?

00:10:27.531 --> 00:10:28.773
- Yes, indeed.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.860
Here's one right here.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:33.010
- Yeah, I love y'all.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:35.201
- More than 40 years, almost 50.

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:38.725
(Jane whispering)

00:10:38.725 --> 00:10:40.250
50 years.
- Oh my God.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.550
(all laughing)

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:43.553
She said, wait.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.220
Over that much time there's obviously been

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.190
ups and downs in your life?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.650
How do you think the other
has kind of helped you

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.970
in not only your career,
maybe your personal life?

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:58.010
- What I did is I learned,

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:01.840
because she had already
examined her life so thoroughly,

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.330
written like three books about her life.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.659
- About myself.

00:11:06.659 --> 00:11:09.500
(all laughing)
- I love you.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.500
- About your life, really.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:15.210
And so I just chucked searching my life

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.570
and I just adapted, I jumped on her.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.800
- And molded.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.910
- I jumped on her and I just
thought I would live her life

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.380
kind of vicariously
because she'd already done

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.453
all the research.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.730
- You're that kid in school,

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.007
looking at the paper on the
other one, that's amazing.

